<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <Itf Name="IDictionary" Id="{57e81792-3900-4cad-861e-9c1a745a287a}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Associates generic keys with values.</summary>
<description>
SetGeneric retains an existing matching key and replaces its value.
SetGeneric preserves disposal responsibility when the same allocation is reused; transferred
caller-side owning aliases must not be released again.
SetCopy prepares owned copies and cleans up prepared copies on failure before acceptance.
Try lookup/removal operations contain exceptions without rolling back partial effects.
Generic query arguments are borrowed by default.
Explicitly requested release in Try operations is attempted even after lookup failure; caller-side
owning aliases are not reset.
OBJECT keys are permitted when their descriptors refer to live Object instances.
A borrowed key (IsMemoryOwner = FALSE) is not owned or destroyed by the dictionary; its owner must
keep it alive for every operation that may access the stored key.
An owned key must not be deleted or transferred to another owner through a caller-side alias.
While a key is stored, do not change data used by the active comparison rules, its equality/hash
results, or equality-relevant comparer configuration.
Remove the entry before such a change, then insert it again.
Queries and callbacks must not mutate keys or reenter collection mutation.
Do not use explicit query release to dispose of a stored key or other storage still retained by the
collection.
An address-based identity index must be rebuilt after address relocation; stale indices must not be
used.
Borrowing does not pin an object or extend its lifetime.
A copied object has its own identity; lookup using the original requires an equality strategy under
which original and copy are equal.
Default OBJECT lookup delegates to Object.Equals/GetHashCode; fields unrelated to equality/hash may
change.
Discard and populate the index again after equality-relevant address relocation before further
lookup.
Lookup uses one equality/hash strategy fixed for the collection lifetime; zero selects GENERIC_VALUE
default equality and hashing.
A custom comparer is borrowed, stays alive and retains stable equality-relevant configuration.
Empty descriptors are supported unless rejected by a validator.
No entry or enumeration order is guaranteed; a position is a current storage slot, not a sorted
rank.
Do not modify stored descriptors through returned references.
</description>
*)
(*
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: © 2026 Oleksandr Tiutyk <trofimich@gmail.com>
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
License: https://opensource.org/license/mit
*)

INTERFACE IDictionary EXTENDS IReadOnlyDictionary]]></Declaration>
    <Method Name="Clear" Id="{b1563b71-bd6a-4263-830c-984583112e42}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Removes all entries and releases owned payload.</summary>
<description>
Disposal is best effort.
Dynamic entry and index storage are released; static capacity and lifetime comparer/validators are
retained.
References, positions and active enumeration are invalidated.
Cleanup callbacks must not reenter mutation.
</description>
*)
METHOD Clear : IDictionary]]></Declaration>
    </Method>
    <Property Name="KeyValidator" Id="{92f9f0be-92c2-4492-ae57-6e7c17023a23}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Exposes the configured key validator.</summary>
<description>
Borrowed optional reference fixed at initialization. Zero means no validator. The collection does not own or release it.
</description>
*)
{attribute 'monitoring' := 'call'}
PROPERTY FINAL KeyValidator : TOF_Core.IGenericValueValidator]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{42575a64-1c39-4806-863c-d88935d3981e}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[]]></Declaration>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Method Name="RemoveAt" Id="{a1586ec5-b74e-4671-96ad-ae4197067882}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Removes the entry at a current storage position.</summary>
<description>
The index must be within Length and is not a sorted rank.
Removal invalidates positions and references as entries are compacted; owned payload disposal is
best effort.
Invalid indices raise an exception.
</description>
*)
METHOD RemoveAt : IDictionary
VAR_INPUT
	index : DINT;
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="SetCopy" Id="{f13fbbaa-2923-411c-9a7c-638998bcf36d}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Copies source key and value storage and stores the prepared copies.</summary>
<description>
Original arguments remain borrowed.
Object copies follow ICloneable; other payload is copied as bytes.
Prepared copies are released if copying or insertion fails before ownership is accepted.
Exceptions propagate after cleanup, without clearing terminal allocation state.
The index output is meaningful only on success.
</description>
*)
//!<param name="key">Borrowed source key.</param>
//!<param name="value">Borrowed source value.</param>
//!<param name="keyIsObject">Explicitly interprets the key as object storage.</param>
//!<param name="valueIsObject">Explicitly interprets the value as object storage.</param>
METHOD SetCopy : IDictionary
VAR_INPUT
	key : ANY;
	value : ANY;
	keyIsObject : BOOL := FALSE;
	valueIsObject : BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
	index : DINT;
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="SetGeneric" Id="{9a515aa5-db44-4d5d-9fbd-7695318ffa56}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Stores a key-value pair, retaining the existing key when a matching entry is updated.</summary>
<description>
Uses the lifetime equality/hash strategy, with no ordering guarantee.
Empty descriptors are permitted unless rejected by a validator.
A successful call accepts owned arguments; borrowed payload must remain alive while stored.
Validation, lookup and growth occur before acceptance; failure before acceptance leaves incoming
ownership with the caller.
An unused owned incoming key and a displaced owned value are released after the new entry is
installed, unless their allocation is retained.
Reusing the same allocation preserves existing ownership or accepts incoming ownership; it never
returns ownership implicitly.
When key and value alias one allocation, the key descriptor holds the pair's disposal
responsibility.
Input descriptor copies are not reset in the caller: transferred owning aliases must not be released
or reused as owners.
Aliases must describe the same allocation with compatible disposal semantics; overlapping owned
ranges and ownership already held by another entry or owner are not supported.
Callbacks must not mutate or reenter this collection.
Cleanup is best effort through GENERIC_VALUE.Release and does not guarantee successful deallocation.
The index output is valid only on success.
</description>
*)
//!<param name="key">Incoming key descriptor; owned storage is transferred on success.</param>
//!<param name="value">Incoming value descriptor; owned storage is transferred on success.</param>
METHOD SetGeneric : IDictionary
VAR_INPUT
	key : TOF_Core.GENERIC_VALUE;
	value : TOF_Core.GENERIC_VALUE;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
	index : DINT;
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="TryRemoveByGenericKey" Id="{ed98c14c-8b20-4e0c-b155-925d2858a0a4}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Attempts to remove a matching entry.</summary>
<description>
Returns the collection for chaining. removed is TRUE only after the matching entry has been removed;
FALSE means no completed removal was reported.
Removal is not transactional and does not prove successful destruction of an owned payload.
Catches exceptions without propagating them or clearing terminal allocation state.
Partial changes are not rolled back.
The query is borrowed by default.
When releaseKey is explicitly TRUE, attempts to release the supplied generic argument after
lookup/removal even on failure.
The caller must have disposal rights and must not reuse aliases of an owned argument after release.
</description>
*)
METHOD TryRemoveByGenericKey : IDictionary
VAR_INPUT
	key : TOF_Core.GENERIC_VALUE;
	releaseKey : BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
	removed : BOOL;
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="TryRemoveByKey" Id="{2539d3ce-1d3f-4331-818e-1181097b6910}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Attempts to remove a matching entry.</summary>
<description>
Returns the collection for chaining. removed is TRUE only after the matching entry has been removed;
FALSE means no completed removal was reported.
Removal is not transactional and does not prove successful destruction of an owned payload.
Catches exceptions without propagating them or clearing terminal allocation state.
Partial changes are not rolled back.
The raw ANY argument is borrowed without cloning or ownership transfer. keyIsObject = TRUE requires
a live Object function-block instance, not a pointer or interface variable.
FALSE uses ordinary runtime type mapping.
The caller keeps the query storage alive for the call.
</description>
*)
//!<param name="keyIsObject">Explicitly interprets the raw argument as a live Object instance.</param>
METHOD TryRemoveByKey : IDictionary
VAR_INPUT
	key : ANY;
	keyIsObject : BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
	removed : BOOL;
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
    </Method>
    <Property Name="ValueValidator" Id="{a4d8a2d8-7635-4460-bcb5-588610d86052}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Exposes the configured value validator.</summary>
<description>
Borrowed optional reference fixed at initialization. Zero means no validator. The collection does not own or release it.
</description>
*)
{attribute 'monitoring' := 'call'}
PROPERTY FINAL ValueValidator : TOF_Core.IGenericValueValidator]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{31d569db-ff61-4467-bd5c-a827d305ce71}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[]]></Declaration>
      </Get>
    </Property>
  </Itf>
</TcPlcObject>
